title: Rename and move prefabs
intro: Prefabs can be renamed and moved between folders in the Assets panel. Every copy stays linked to its prefab, in every scene and inside other prefabs.
project: Platformer | Prefab Moves

chapter: A gem prefab | Placed twice
look: 8, -2, 4
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Gem
set: Transform.Position = 5, -3, 0
set: Sprite.Tint = #29ADFF
set: Sprite.Size = 0.6, 0.6
menu: Entity > Save as Prefab
key: Ctrl+D
rename: Gem 2
set: Transform.Position = 7.5, -3, 0
save
expectlinked: Gem 2 = Prefabs/Gem.prefab
explain: asset:Prefabs/Gem.prefab | The prefab | Two gems, both copies of the Gem prefab in the Prefabs folder.

chapter: Rename it | Right-click it in Assets
assetmenu: Prefabs/Gem.prefab > Rename...
prompt: Blue Gem
expectfile: Prefabs/Blue Gem.prefab
expectlinked: Gem = Prefabs/Blue Gem.prefab
expectlinked: Gem 2 = Prefabs/Blue Gem.prefab
explain: asset:Prefabs/Blue Gem.prefab | Renamed | Rename on its menu gives the prefab a new name, and every copy stays linked to it.
select: Gem 2
explain: prefabnote | Copy of the Blue Gem prefab | So saving the prefab still updates them all.

chapter: Move it | Drag it onto a folder
assetmenu: Main.scene > New Folder...
prompt: Pickups
assetdrop: Prefabs/Blue Gem.prefab > Pickups
expectfile: Pickups/Blue Gem.prefab
expectlinked: Gem = Pickups/Blue Gem.prefab
expectlinked: Gem 2 = Pickups/Blue Gem.prefab
explain: asset:Pickups/Blue Gem.prefab | Moved | Dragging it onto a folder moves it there, and again its copies follow.
say: Copies in other scenes and inside other prefabs are relinked too. A script spawns a prefab by its name, so a rename means changing those names as well.
